WEBVTT

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:15.890
Josephine!

00:00:18.950 --> 00:00:22.100
You're going to give that to me?
 Thanks!

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:24.490
Josephine!

00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:28.120
- Yamashiro-san!
- I'm sorry.

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:32.580
When I don't keep an eye on her, she runs off.

00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:36.250
On top of that, she always has something in her mouth.

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:40.610
- Is that so?
- Don't do it again.

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:44.050
Come, let's go, Josephine.

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:56.950
Hello, this is Cafe Hakobune.

00:00:57.840 --> 00:00:58.960
I want to order take-out.

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:02.520
One fish and chips with ketchup.

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:05.300
- Fish and chips?
- Yea.

00:01:05.870 --> 00:01:07.460
- Fish and chips.
- Certainly!

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:11.760
We have a take-out order, Kanako.

00:01:11.950 --> 00:01:16.060
Let's get started on it, Yayoi. 
 What is this dish called?

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:20.460
It's --- I forget the name of the dish.

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:22.880
Can you tell me what kind of dish it is?

00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:24.850
I sure will.

00:01:26.030 --> 00:01:28.420
It is a story about a master and a servant.

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:33.930
The master wore a mantle and a button of wisdom and heritage.

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:38.170
At times, wielding a warm baiser and, at other times, a cold sigh...

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:40.370
...made people his captive.

00:01:40.780 --> 00:01:43.870
Once again, having his servants follow him...

00:01:43.940 --> 00:01:46.230
...the master heads to the feast.

00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:49.100
What a captivating dish!

00:01:49.190 --> 00:01:53.680
- Do you know of such a dish?
- Yes, of course.

00:03:25.170 --> 00:03:28.290
Computer Grandma

00:03:28.930 --> 00:03:30.580
I'm going to deliver this.

00:03:33.770 --> 00:03:36.760
It's hot; I feel like I'm going to melt.

00:03:36.760 --> 00:03:39.020
If it's like this, we won't have any customers.

00:03:40.490 --> 00:03:42.430
The air conditioning isn't on?

00:03:44.150 --> 00:03:48.070
We, as ghosts, are sweating.

00:03:48.070 --> 00:03:50.840
It must be really hot.

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:54.410
Oh, right. You guys are sweating.

00:03:54.860 --> 00:03:56.610
Yes, thanks to the heat.

00:03:56.640 --> 00:04:01.350
Both Yayoi and I, our shadows have become darker recently.

00:04:01.610 --> 00:04:07.380
Spending time with you guys from Hakobune, it feels like my existence is becoming great.

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:10.240
It feels like 35°C.

00:04:14.700 --> 00:04:16.960
Wow! You're right on!

00:04:17.920 --> 00:04:22.700
Yea! I can sense it for some reason.

00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:27.540
It's nostalgic.
 The beaming sun...

00:04:27.890 --> 00:04:32.100
...where the heat and light are rushing at me.

00:04:35.980 --> 00:04:40.060
Well, let's think about turning on the air conditioner.

00:04:41.620 --> 00:04:44.800
- Hey, Kamigamo, where's the remote?
- I don't know.

00:04:45.540 --> 00:04:50.760
Well, the Master always has the remote and won't let go of it.

00:04:51.140 --> 00:04:56.620
- Really?
- When is the last time you adjusted the air conditioner?

00:04:56.970 --> 00:05:02.260
I think it was when I was drinking here--- maybe, maybe not.

00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:04.680
When was it? Last night?

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:08.380
It might have been last night -- maybe, maybe not.

00:05:08.660 --> 00:05:10.730
How careless!

00:05:13.540 --> 00:05:17.010
36°C, 36.5°C.

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:27.740
Anyway, we have to find that remote! I can't run a business in this heat!

00:05:28.280 --> 00:05:32.650
- Roger that! Let's go, Hajime-chan! 
- Roger!

00:05:34.620 --> 00:05:36.660
Could this be?!

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:45.360
This is?!

00:05:47.050 --> 00:05:49.500
It is a story about a master and a servant.

00:05:50.100 --> 00:05:55.040
The master wore a mantle and a button of wisdom and heritage.

00:05:55.420 --> 00:05:59.600
At times, wielding a warm baiser and, at other times, a cold sigh...

00:05:59.920 --> 00:06:01.920
...made people his captive.

00:06:02.590 --> 00:06:05.710
Once again, having his servants follow him...

00:06:05.870 --> 00:06:08.170
...the master heads to the feast.

00:06:08.800 --> 00:06:10.140
It's that kind of dish.

00:06:10.840 --> 00:06:13.840
These are fish and chips?!

00:06:17.280 --> 00:06:21.130
- These are all the remotes we found. 
- Which one is it?

00:06:21.350 --> 00:06:23.330
Let's test all of them!

00:06:23.650 --> 00:06:25.530
This one seems like it.

00:06:29.890 --> 00:06:33.810
Um, let's try this one next!

00:06:36.550 --> 00:06:41.450
- Why is the chair moving?!
- I don't get it. How about this one?

00:06:43.840 --> 00:06:45.980
- Oh, sorry, sorry.
- Can't believe you.

00:06:46.200 --> 00:06:48.110
- Someone get a towel.
- OK.

00:06:49.100 --> 00:06:50.530
38°C.

00:06:52.980 --> 00:06:55.050
- What is it?
- Oh, nothing.

00:06:55.050 --> 00:06:58.210
- You're weird, Hajime-chan.
- Could this be?!

00:06:58.340 --> 00:07:00.370
Let's try this next!

00:07:04.130 --> 00:07:05.470
I'm sorry, Hajime-chan!

00:07:05.760 --> 00:07:10.190
Don't worry. It doesn't phase me. Let's try the next one!

00:07:11.870 --> 00:07:13.470
I'm back.

00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:16.750
What is this?

00:07:22.800 --> 00:07:24.580
All of them have been wrong.

00:07:24.900 --> 00:07:27.350
All we have left are these three.

00:07:27.770 --> 00:07:30.700
It's good to wipe the floor with the water that you washed rice with.

00:07:32.360 --> 00:07:35.700
- How about this one?
- That one looks way off.

00:07:38.950 --> 00:07:42.140
- Arashiyama Sayoko.
- Let's go!

00:07:51.500 --> 00:07:53.440
There's something wrong with that one! Stop her!

00:07:53.700 --> 00:07:58.440
- 39°C.
- Arashi-san, hurry! Arashi-san!

00:07:59.620 --> 00:08:04.050
- 39.5°C.
- Arashi-san!

00:08:06.060 --> 00:08:07.490
Arashi-san, what's wrong?

00:08:09.180 --> 00:08:12.460
- Arashi-san.
- Ten rules of the Arashiyama family.

00:08:13.700 --> 00:08:15.140
Family rule number one.

00:08:16.090 --> 00:08:18.130
The daughter of the Arashiyama household...

00:08:19.090 --> 00:08:21.860
...must be strong and silent at all times.

00:08:24.310 --> 00:08:27.050
Could this be?

00:08:27.430 --> 00:08:30.460
- You got her started! 
- Started?

00:08:32.310 --> 00:08:36.190
How terrifying! Something terrifying is going to happen!

00:08:36.540 --> 00:08:38.900
-What do you mean by "terrifying?" 
- Well...

00:08:40.430 --> 00:08:42.590
As a young girl, Arashi...

00:08:42.690 --> 00:08:45.270
...was raised with strict rules.

00:08:45.810 --> 00:08:47.630
As a daughter of the Arashiyama household...

00:08:47.820 --> 00:08:52.920
...she was not allowed to complain and say things like "it's hot" or "it's cold."

00:08:55.750 --> 00:09:00.620
For years, Arashi faithfully obeyed those commands.

00:09:02.820 --> 00:09:05.980
But it didn't mean she was OK.

00:09:07.760 --> 00:09:11.550
Experiencing the summer heat over and over, Arashi's complaint...

00:09:11.900 --> 00:09:14.070
...has been compiling deep inside her.

00:09:14.860 --> 00:09:19.770
- It's about to all explode now!
- What happens when it explodes?!

00:09:20.150 --> 00:09:23.110
- She's going to start singing the "Warabe Tune."
- Warabe Tune?

00:09:24.260 --> 00:09:28.050
When she's done with the tune, it's going to be a nightmare!

00:09:28.660 --> 00:09:31.940
The "Emperor of Fire's Tragedy" will reoccur!

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:36.940
- "Emperor of Fire's Tragedy"
- Don't make me say anymore!

00:09:40.440 --> 00:09:44.550
Noooo! Noooo!

00:09:45.440 --> 00:09:50.540
Family rule number 2: Faith without action is useless.

00:09:50.700 --> 00:09:53.720
No! We have to hurry and cool the store down, or else Arashi-san will...

00:09:53.720 --> 00:09:56.150
- What are you doing?
- It's dangerous.

00:09:57.520 --> 00:09:58.380
Yasaka!

00:10:00.990 --> 00:10:05.610
- I told you so. 
- Our last hope!

00:10:05.610 --> 00:10:08.380
- Hold on, Yasaka! 
- Don't panic!

00:10:09.970 --> 00:10:13.570
There's no guarantee this one is the one.

00:10:13.950 --> 00:10:16.150
What would happen if I press this?

00:10:16.720 --> 00:10:21.250
I might bring disaster to Hakobune.

00:10:21.760 --> 00:10:25.320
Family rule number 3: If there is a storm and a flower...

00:10:25.610 --> 00:10:27.780
...always seek the storm.

00:10:28.700 --> 00:10:32.590
But I can't just leave Arashi-san like this.

00:10:33.770 --> 00:10:38.070
What should I do?! I will...

00:10:42.490 --> 00:10:46.760
Natsu No Arashi!

00:10:48.740 --> 00:10:52.530
What should I do?! I will...

00:10:57.270 --> 00:10:58.900
What if that happens?!

00:11:00.680 --> 00:11:02.500
I don't know what to do!

00:11:05.560 --> 00:11:06.860
Family rule number five.

00:11:19.830 --> 00:11:24.540
- It seems really deep. 
- It's more like a cave than a basement.

00:11:24.540 --> 00:11:25.910
How is Arashi doing?

00:11:26.100 --> 00:11:28.710
It seems to be working.

00:11:28.910 --> 00:11:34.580
- Family rule number 11: Tempura should be eaten with salt.
- Arashi-san!

00:11:35.660 --> 00:11:39.670
Should we go in? It might be better than up here.

00:11:46.780 --> 00:11:50.660
Don't worry, Arashi-san. I'm here with you.

00:11:52.290 --> 00:11:54.990
It's pretty cool inside this cave.

00:11:56.010 --> 00:11:58.240
This will ease Arashi-san a little bit.

00:12:00.120 --> 00:12:01.590
What is this?!

00:12:02.130 --> 00:12:04.360
A hot spring might be gushing out!

00:12:04.610 --> 00:12:08.370
Hot spring?! Why doesn't it come out in the winter?!

00:12:08.850 --> 00:12:12.070
No way! A water heater broke somewhere.

00:12:12.480 --> 00:12:14.580
This might be worse than inside the store.

00:12:14.840 --> 00:12:18.570
- Oh, it's hot! It's hot!
- No!

00:12:18.920 --> 00:12:20.860
It's not hot!

00:12:24.460 --> 00:12:27.040
- Iron claw?!
- Yasaka!

00:12:27.100 --> 00:12:29.840
Is this the "Emperor of Fire's Tragedy?"

00:12:30.130 --> 00:12:33.890
No, this is only a warning.

00:12:34.650 --> 00:12:37.070
Warning?! This is?

00:12:37.140 --> 00:12:40.450
The terror that awaits us beyond this...

00:12:41.020 --> 00:12:44.970
...is hell that none of us can avoid!

00:12:45.290 --> 00:12:49.690
The nightmare of that day... that fateful day in the summer here again!

00:12:55.390 --> 00:12:59.790
46°C, 47°C, 48°C.

00:13:02.330 --> 00:13:05.040
49°C, 50°C.

00:13:06.860 --> 00:13:08.190
It's not hot!

00:13:08.700 --> 00:13:12.620
What should we do, Kaya-san?! If we don't do anything, Arashi-san and Yasaka are...

00:13:13.040 --> 00:13:16.920
But what should we do? 
 I have an idea!

00:13:18.290 --> 00:13:23.130
Here we go. "Underground, Chikako showed her strength!"

00:13:25.140 --> 00:13:27.910
- How was that?
- Negative 5°C.

00:13:34.760 --> 00:13:36.320
Are you OK, Yasaka?

00:13:37.600 --> 00:13:39.700
Arashiyama-senpai stopped!

00:13:40.020 --> 00:13:43.430
Back in the days, when I said something funny...

00:13:46.710 --> 00:13:50.340
<i>It gets cool when I listen to your story, Kaya!</i>

00:13:51.480 --> 00:13:53.490
I thought it might work.

00:13:53.940 --> 00:13:56.170
Oh, I get it.

00:13:59.290 --> 00:14:03.840
I want beer. Someone get me a beer!

00:14:04.190 --> 00:14:06.420
I just want to drink a draft!

00:14:07.350 --> 00:14:10.690
What are you mumbling about?!

00:14:10.820 --> 00:14:12.440
It's so ho...

00:14:14.550 --> 00:14:17.030
I was like... wow! I'm surprised!

00:14:19.230 --> 00:14:20.410
51°C.

00:14:23.370 --> 00:14:25.950
Oh, it's just a breeze.

00:14:26.170 --> 00:14:30.630
It makes that echo off of the rocks. Nothing to worry about.

00:14:31.020 --> 00:14:32.890
Oh, OK.

00:14:33.370 --> 00:14:35.730
That means this cave is...

00:14:35.860 --> 00:14:39.780
...connected to the outside.

00:14:40.920 --> 00:14:41.940
I want to hold you!

00:14:46.240 --> 00:14:48.250
It's a Brown Hirata Anisodactylus Signatus.

00:14:48.820 --> 00:14:51.690
It's a type that lives underground and aboveground.

00:14:54.010 --> 00:14:57.360
You need more training, Cadet Kamigamo!

00:15:04.210 --> 00:15:07.550
- Ouch! Why?!
- Don't touch me!

00:15:14.460 --> 00:15:16.950
Kaboom!

00:15:17.430 --> 00:15:21.500
- Kaboom?!
- Arashi has exploded!

00:15:22.940 --> 00:15:26.700
"The sun is shining"

00:15:26.950 --> 00:15:30.740
"Ten spirits are here"

00:15:30.930 --> 00:15:33.230
- "Went down to the river to play"
- Arashi-san!

00:15:33.580 --> 00:15:36.000
The "Warabe Tune" started!

00:15:36.190 --> 00:15:38.640
She's in her final stage now.

00:15:38.990 --> 00:15:42.690
"The sun is shining"

00:15:42.940 --> 00:15:46.610
"Nine spirits are here"

00:15:46.920 --> 00:15:50.910
"Chasing after cicadas"

00:15:50.970 --> 00:15:53.420
When she sings that song to the end...

00:15:53.420 --> 00:15:55.940
the "Emperor of Fire's Tragedy" is going to strike again!

00:15:55.970 --> 00:15:59.280
If that happens, no one will be able to...

00:15:59.280 --> 00:16:02.760
"Eight spirits are here"

00:16:03.170 --> 00:16:07.310
"Chasing after cicadas"

00:16:07.310 --> 00:16:10.620
"Seven spirits are left"

00:16:10.620 --> 00:16:14.350
- There's only seven more! 
- Kaya-san, again!

00:16:15.660 --> 00:16:20.120
I got it. "I shoot ten shots freely!"

00:16:22.730 --> 00:16:26.580
"The sun is shining"

00:16:26.580 --> 00:16:30.340
"Ten spirits are here"

00:16:30.600 --> 00:16:34.320
- "Went down to the river to play"
- It's back to ten!

00:16:34.450 --> 00:16:36.970
"Ten" for "gun" I get it.

00:16:37.060 --> 00:16:39.900
We have to take her back to the store, hurry!

00:16:45.600 --> 00:16:47.770
Draft beer, draft beer.

00:16:47.800 --> 00:16:52.320
- Is this really the right way?
- I can't see anything.

00:16:58.820 --> 00:17:01.720
What kind of phenomenon is this?!

00:17:01.810 --> 00:17:04.900
An alien or UMA...

00:17:05.090 --> 00:17:09.810
...I think our fears are creating a mirage psychologically.

00:17:10.410 --> 00:17:12.520
It's not a mirage!

00:17:12.710 --> 00:17:15.480
- Could this be...
- ...a monster?!

00:17:17.580 --> 00:17:19.650
You're not there-- you don't exist!

00:17:19.680 --> 00:17:22.550
It's just a mirage!

00:17:25.930 --> 00:17:29.810
I don't care! I'm going to protect Arashi-san!

00:17:38.510 --> 00:17:39.690
Yayoi!

00:17:41.540 --> 00:17:45.360
Josephine! Why are you here?

00:17:47.330 --> 00:17:52.110
- What is that? 
- Yes! Draft beer!

00:17:52.780 --> 00:17:57.140
- The remote! Hurry up! 
- Just a little bit more, Arashi-san!

00:17:57.400 --> 00:18:01.190
"The sun is shining"

00:18:01.410 --> 00:18:04.920
"Five spirits are here"

00:18:05.360 --> 00:18:09.280
"Slipping while climbing a tree"

00:18:09.570 --> 00:18:11.130
I'm counting on you, air conditioner!

00:18:14.660 --> 00:18:17.530
- Backing, backing. 
- What?!

00:18:18.840 --> 00:18:20.840
This one isn't it either!

00:18:20.840 --> 00:18:24.670
"The sun is shining"

00:18:24.820 --> 00:18:28.520
"Four spirits are here"

00:18:28.930 --> 00:18:31.770
It's down to four! Four, Kanako!

00:18:32.570 --> 00:18:37.180
I will be with you till the end, Yayoi!

00:18:37.180 --> 00:18:40.620
- Please, professor!
 - Leave it to me!

00:18:41.930 --> 00:18:46.490
"The twins cover the two again!"

00:18:48.520 --> 00:18:52.350
"The sun is shining"

00:18:52.570 --> 00:18:56.170
"Two spirits are here"

00:18:56.330 --> 00:18:58.620
- Two spirits?!
- It decreased!

00:19:00.600 --> 00:19:04.070
"One spirit is left"

00:19:05.790 --> 00:19:10.440
- "Quadruple decker!"
- Kaya-san, there's no time for that!

00:19:10.690 --> 00:19:15.380
- Kaya-san! 
- "Sun is shining"

00:19:15.500 --> 00:19:18.980
"One spirit is here"

00:19:19.070 --> 00:19:20.820
Arashi-san!

00:19:22.070 --> 00:19:25.920
What's up. What's going on here!

00:19:26.270 --> 00:19:29.680
- Are you trying to build character here? 
- Shut up!

00:19:29.710 --> 00:19:33.280
- We can't find the remote! 
- Remote control?!

00:19:35.000 --> 00:19:36.820
Are you talking about this?!

00:19:37.040 --> 00:19:41.340
That's where it is! GO!

00:19:48.000 --> 00:19:49.840
Oh, Arashi-san?!

00:20:22.180 --> 00:20:26.600
Josephine, how many times do I have to tell her?!

00:20:29.090 --> 00:20:33.170
"Blowing up fireworks"

00:20:33.200 --> 00:20:36.990
"Everyone is all gone!"

00:22:12.650 --> 00:22:14.720
How are you doing, Yayoi?

00:22:15.000 --> 00:22:17.200
I'm doing well, Kanako.

00:22:17.520 --> 00:22:19.880
That's good to hear.

00:22:20.100 --> 00:22:24.880
- I read another book. 
- What was the book called?

00:22:25.010 --> 00:22:28.760
It was-- I forget the title.

00:22:28.960 --> 00:22:31.280
Can you tell me what the story was about?

00:22:31.280 --> 00:22:33.380
I sure will.

00:22:35.390 --> 00:22:37.910
It was a legend about this creature.

00:22:38.380 --> 00:22:42.370
It came from an egg that an ordinary boy found.

00:22:42.430 --> 00:22:44.850
The creature was something out of this world.

00:22:45.360 --> 00:22:48.130
Having a barren and cold head like the wilderness.

00:22:48.420 --> 00:22:51.000
The large eyes shine like silver plates.

00:22:51.320 --> 00:22:55.680
The wide split mouth ruthlessly eats up its prey.

00:22:56.130 --> 00:23:00.490
At times, the creature disappears and flies into the night.

00:23:00.650 --> 00:23:02.850
No one can stop this creature.

00:23:03.290 --> 00:23:07.150
One day, the family of the creature comes to the boy.

00:23:07.850 --> 00:23:10.880
This is how their ordinary day gets destroyed.

00:23:11.070 --> 00:23:13.870
Everything is swallowed up in chaos.

00:23:14.350 --> 00:23:15.940
Forever and ever.

00:23:17.250 --> 00:23:20.080
What a scary story.

00:23:20.210 --> 00:23:24.640
There's an unique cry that the creature's brother lets out.

00:23:24.920 --> 00:23:26.640
Can I hear it?

00:23:28.650 --> 00:23:29.380
"Bakkeratta!"

00:23:30.750 --> 00:23:34.450
- When I say air conditioning... 
- There are some places that are too cold.

00:23:34.510 --> 00:23:39.670
I like getting it really cold in the summer and wearing warm clothes and doing the opposite in the winter.

00:23:39.670 --> 00:23:43.460
- You're so harsh towards the Earth.
- Wake up early tomorrow!

00:23:45.080 --> 00:23:47.950
See you next week!
